00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:38,000
cu cek kir ne e va wî kî o o likît kî cucak, vê re cê kerne
ma ni hew ti kev e, cêk varin vo xen.
 
Look what they did, they did this like a trough for birds,
meaning the birds can come and drink water.

73
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:47,000
lî hê va ketî yên bi non na ha ey bov yuy yên ecay ye de, ha
ma nê cek we m ba xen rê nê xide re ma, xa lî giyo ye cî ox
cin at e xud e ko bel ko
 
They put bread here for the dead to have some, meaning the
birds will come and drink, may God have mercy on them, may
his place be paradise, may God accept it.

74
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:56,000
aa haw vî ci lê, varî je we zimiş kîn a ne herî ci. a ve nê
e he diyate nê bi ri kî mo bî zêr i vone ci li der one xe
der me qalîg ke
 
ah this one from the side, come side, we will write it, for
everyone. This is a gift, with a brotherly soul, they wrote
it, may God have mercy on him.

75
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,000
ci ox e cî nati.
 
May his place be paradise.

76
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Zeynet be. De ka, ha.
 
May it be an adornment. Come on.

77
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Mistefa Mihemed Mûsa.
 
Mustafa Muhammed Musa.

78
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Mistefa Mihemed Mûsa. Dê em ka evê jî em herin bi cî bikin
apê Ebdoyê.
 
Mustafa Muhammed Musa. Let's go and plant this one too,
uncle Abdo.

79
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Koma ra man darên ha, hazir?
 
Are these trees ready for the group?

80
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Erê bi Xwedê şeş heb em nuha dê li tirban da biçînin.
 
Yes, by God, we are going to plant six of them in the graves
right now.

81
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Bes xwesteka xelkê me ew e, me ji merivan xwest ku dê tê di
ortê de qut nekin.
 
But our people's request is, we asked people not to cut them
in the middle.

82
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Min ha şevê din li tirban ew me yê qut kirîye, qesdî ewa.
 
The other night at the graves, someone cut it,
intentionally.

83
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Yanî li vir berê dar qut kirine, darê çîye sînûber e çiye ha
wa.
 
Meaning, they used to cut trees here, is it a pine tree or
what.

84
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Ev çiye Loqman, ev çûçeng e?
 
What is this Luqman, is this a spruce?

85
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Serwîç e.
 
It's a cypress.

86
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Serwîç. Ev pir dereng mezin dibe.
 
Cypress. This grows very late.

87
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Ne wey? Neh deh sal gere kê xwîna ser çîçkê xwe xelas ke.
 
Right? It needs nine, ten years to finish its sapling stage.

88
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Ka her yekê dorekê tê de berkin. Tabî ha vana her sêk, ha
vana her sêk in we yek li vir e.
 
Let everyone put a layer (of soil) in it. Look, these three,
these are all three and one is here.

89
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Û ev din jî li jêr in. Ewa dê tê jêr ne. Ev bi ziravan jî li
darana ye.
 
And the others are down there. Yes, they will be down there.
These thin ones are also from trees.

90
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Saetekê em geriyan heta me bi cî kirin. Erê welleh.
 
We walked around for an hour until we planted them. Yes, by
God.

91
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Ewa hemû de yê têne her yekê dorek sê cê din ber sere.
 
Yes, all of them will have a layer of soil thrown on top in
three places.

92
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Çîçkê gavş e Ebdîn? Talbîz e wile?
 
What kind of sapling is it, Abdin? Is it Talbiz?

93
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Talbîze wile, talbîz e lê qertaxa darê naxce ye, ji sedî
sed.
 
It's Talbiz indeed, it's Talbiz but the branch is a very
successful tree, 100%.

94
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Erê, erd şil e rutûba xwe heye.
 
Yes, the ground is wet, it has its moisture.

95
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Ya şîk o çîçkê wî da hinekî jê dûr xe, ê Hemed. Ewa ev me
apê wê de ha front.
 
Take its sapling and put it a bit further from it, oh Ahmed.
Look, we put this in the front.

96
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Rast kevir ha jêr, ewa borîya çemberî ye vana çûçik pê va
ye, xweyê erdê ev av dikî.
 
Straight down, under the stone, this is the hoop pipe that
the bird is attached to, the owner of the land waters this.

97
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Ewa wê jê ketiye xwarê, ev me re rind e ew nagihê. Me go em
ê pê ve lehim kin sibe da.
 
It has fallen down, it's good for us, it doesn't reach it.
We said we will weld it tomorrow.

98
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Yanî minteqeya ha ne kavir e. Lê dîsa kavir av dibe. Em ê
çêkin sibe da.
 
I mean, this area is not rocky. But the rocks get watered.
We will fix it tomorrow.

99
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Dorê sê cî rind in, wele sîc hene. Vana yekî vir çandiye
xwelî ser kirîye. Vaye dara sîc e yê wdîye.
 
The surrounding of three places are good, well, there is
soil here. Someone planted one here and put dirt on it.
Look, this is a soil tree.

100
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Haye dara sîc e yê.
 
Look, this is a soil tree.

101
00:11:55,000 --> 00:12:02,000
Ko were hezet, ...
 
Come here, hazet, ...

102
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Maşellah çi cewekî xweş e. Lê hey. Cew ewr e. Dê sibe
maşellah baranê cem e kebz kir. Me go yanê em nikarin herin.
 
Mashallah, what a nice weather. Oh hey. Cloudy weather. But
tomorrow, Mashallah, the rain will pour down. We said we
wouldn't be able to go.

103
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Hemû vê sibê zû rabûn min dît çûn Efrîn, ne tenê dara sîc e
hûn anîn.
 
Everyone got up early this morning, I saw them going to
Afrin, not only bringing a soil tree.

104
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Lê min dar hazir kiribûn, em kî bi we ta re min nelaqand. Me
ta'cîl yanî hûrû kir.
 
But I had prepared the trees, I didn't bother you. We did it
in a hurry.

105
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Hûrû jî baran dîn. Xaka xwe me jî marê dehn kir. Go Ebo
Hezet a ki jî şeş dara biçînim û me jî xwe rêkê xistîyê em
kî wê ne ev e.
 
It was pouring rain. The dirt... Abu Hazat said let's plant
six trees and we got on our way, here we are.

106
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Ta ko vê sibê zû abû makîneyê xwe çûn Efrîn, min dar kirin
paşiya makîneyê xwe, tiştek herrî bû.
 
Until this morning early, getting his machine going to
Afrin, I put the trees in the trunk of his car, everything
got muddy.

107
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Tenê gene baranê lêkiriyê. Çi makîne tiştek herrbî, nosî
naxse li şerê xwe me bidî. Wele, dibê evê makîne çi dike,
ger herrî tê de te da re nav herdê, tê çi bike...
 
It's just that it was raining. The car got all muddy...
Well, saying what is this car doing, it's all muddy inside,
you put it in the ground, what are you doing...

108
00:12:47,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Wele, birakî kê ma Ebo Ebdû, Wele hûrû birakî kê ma me ra
tewasul kir. Dê bê bergê em pîkopekê tara bikirin, raya te
çiye? Ê dê bê yek wekî Ebo Ebdû.
 
Well, a brother of ours, Abu Abdo, well, a brother of ours
contacted us. Saying we should buy a pick-up truck for you,
what is your opinion? Saying someone like Abu Abdo.

109
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Na?
 
No?

110
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Barê pîkopê nîne?
 
Isn't there a load for the pick-up?

111
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Aa. Ewa tenê nava şeye em bi cîbê xwe tên min tişt herrî
kirî. Dar û xes. Lê yek dar e yê din jî, mesel em xezineyê
avê tê kinê.
 
Yeah. That's just the name, we come with our jeep, I made
everything muddy. Trees and lettuce. But one is trees and
the other, for example, we can put a water tank in it.

112
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Îş tiyê re rind e?
 
Is it good for this work?

113
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Welleh saetê kî gind e xweşe dibê kê ma re pîkopekê bikirê.
Sehetê ko gindê xweş Xwedê jî razî be.
 
Well, it would be great if someone bought us a pick-up. It
would be very nice, may God be pleased.

114
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Tabî apo Ebdû eref jî hûrû mirovtî ye.
 
Of course, Uncle Abdo also showed his humanity.

115
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Ebo Mihemed, hûrû me hatine vir maşellah em ho pirin ho
gelekî...
 
Abu Muhammad, we came here, Mashallah, there are many of us,
very much...

116
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:38,000
De de hejmêrin ka kî weki le ko. Dudu, sê sê, çar, pênc,
şeş, heft, heyşt, neh dehe, em dehe me ra hatin ev ro. Dehe
ho ev jî havin e ne?
 
Come on, count them like that. Two, three, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, ten of us came today.
Ten, and these came too, right?

117
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Çike çane wa? Ya li sînga ne.
 
What are those? They are on the chest.

118
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Sed silîm e. Çi kî dan? Avê, avê, yek avê de girin bînin.
 
Good luck. What are they giving? Water, water, grab a water
and bring it.

119
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Maşelleh, evê gundê ha. Pir rind in a!
 
Mashallah, this village here. They are very beautiful!

120
00:13:52,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Ez hatime me, ev gundiyên hanê sewirandin, we yî jor me
sewrandin, bes hawa me lixte di navra çêkirye, ha pir navra
negeriyan. Hem hemwa hacetê ra katrin em çûyîn.
 
I came here, I filmed these villagers and the ones up there,
but we just made a gap in between, we didn't wander around
much in the middle. We were in a hurry, we walked around.

121
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Teswîrê vê gundî me rencê nekirbû. Maşellah çi cewekî xweş
e! Cewek her cî gundî heye. Xwabe nu, xwabe. Ev pira vira
gelek ra zîna derne, welleh sehto miletê gund xweş e.
 
I hadn't properly filmed this village. Mashallah, what a
nice weather! Every village has nice weather. Oh my, oh my.
It's very beautiful here, the doors are... Well, the people
of the village are healthy and well.

122
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:24,000
Nav gund ko kirne, nav tirba ko kirne çira. Û zaretên xwe jî
rind çêkirine. Ewa av din şab ab av din me zû vîde bikin.
 
They worked inside the village, inside the cemetery, why.
And they have made their shrines well. Here, pour water,
pour water so we can finish it quickly.

123
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Ebo Zêrevan, silavên me ji te ra hene. Li welatê der, li
Ewrupayê, li ser vê tirbeyê Şêxmiz da, mewqiê me li vira
silavên me ji te ra hene heta ciyê tu lê. Ebo Zêrevan.
 
Abu Zerevan, we send you our greetings. Abroad, in Europe,
at this grave of Shexmiz, our location is here, we send you
our greetings to where you are. Abu Zerevan.

124
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Tabî li bajarê Ewrupayê ye, em kê nuho darek şemsîyê li
berserê deya te rehmetî kin, Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke, ez wê wî
livolî bigrim. Ewa! Ka çerxê we ne, çerxê me.
 
Of course, he is in the cities of Europe, we will now plant
an umbrella tree at the head of your late mother's grave,
may God have mercy on her, I will take it... Come on! Where
is your wheel/cart, our wheel/cart.

125
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Pêle me ne, pêle tirba me ne.
 
Step on them, step on our graves.

126
00:14:53,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Em kê wê tekin, ew e tov mezin. Dê ewê tov mezin e rinda em
kê te kin, heni dewî hewîn jî nagîne, tişt Ebdoyê êş felafîl
fûl. Kesê giran dî kine ca bî Ebdû. Heta seet deh dewa ya ko
felafilo di qawinîn, fûlo hemso hû jî xizmet milet dikiyo.
 
We will plant it, a big kind. It's a big kind, we will plant
it nicely, even the animals won't reach it, things like
Abdo's pain, falafel, ful. They bring a heavy thing, uncle
Abdo. Until ten o'clock, he fries one falafel, ful, hummus,
he also serves the people.

127
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:32,000
De xwedê rizqê wî bide. Qut ke, qut ke wê qut ke.
 
May God provide for him. Cut it, cut it, cut that.

128
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Ê ew şanbê dorê têk name yê otin, hezet. Dore bi sirati
rindi çêk bike. Xwîn tê, xwîn tê rinde. Dia bikin Ebo
Zerevan Xwedê rehma xwe li deya te ke...
 
We are going to make a border around it, Hazat. Make a good
border for the sapling. Pour water, pour water nicely. Pray
for Abu Zerevan, may God have mercy on your mother...

129
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Ko? Yawaş, milê apo Evdo, te yê da dîneyê, ka. Yawaş hemû de
yawaş. Bes yawaş.
 
Where? Slowly, Uncle Evdo's arm, you look at it, come on.
Slowly, all of it slowly. Just slowly.

130
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Berê ga xera bin e. Barana lêkiriye...
 
Otherwise it will get ruined. It has rained...

131
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Ew me la nîzam bibe apê Evdo, apê Evdo ew na, ew to nibes
bisebtîn e, eva çêke. Lê çêk nabe eva berde hema de vê
berde, wan yê jêr vavo bikirin Evdo.
 
Let us make it properly, uncle Evdo, uncle Evdo... fix it
properly, this is good. But it's not good, let this go, let
all of this go, buy these ones down here, Evdo.

132
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Ewa bişkîne.
 
Here, break it.

133
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Tewer, koşti mlo... Xwedê qebûl ke, me go Xwedê qebûl ke.
 
Axe, ... May God accept it, we said may God accept it.

134
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Mişkîloka me ya çûçik e, em çidikin? Mesela navan pir ji me
dixwazin. Ê tirba... ev heye me re dibêje mesela, li berserî
deya min darekê biçînin, ê din jî tewzî ke.
 
We have a small problem, what do we do? For example, many
want from us in the middle. The grave... there is this,
someone tells us for example, plant one at the head of my
mother's grave and distribute the rest.

135
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:46,000
Ê heye jî, mesela deh dar e, yan pênc dar e, dişîne ji
rehmetyê xwe ya. Em çi dikin em tenê di nav wan tirban de
digerin, yekî ku xwedî hebe li vira...
 
And there are those who, for example, send ten trees or five
trees for their deceased ones. What do we do, we just wander
among those graves, if someone has relatives here...

136
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:55,000
Lê me ra ewel de, wekî gundê ewî ya em çûnê, me ev ku
veşartibû, kevir kirin belê, kevir dînan ser, belê kirin û
xilas. Em çûn ser û mirov çû.
 
But to us in the beginning, like that village we went to,
they buried him, they put rocks, yes, they put rocks on top,
yes, and that's it. We went to the grave and the person
left.

137
00:16:55,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Û me re ew an jî, em tim lê digerin. Tirbe jî pir in ha...
 
And to us those too, we always wander there. There are many
graves too...

138
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Tirsa ye, hezar heye. Dûrek xirtekê çêke. Ka ka, xirtekê
bigire evî giya miyayî, cenet be.
 
...there are thousands. Make a deep hole. Come on, hold the
hole and this grass, may it be paradise.

139
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Bi mehel he, apo Ebdû.
 
With strength, uncle Abdo.

140
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Lê. Derdikeve wele rinde, ava xwe xwerîye, baranê nîne?
 
Yes. It comes out well, it has absorbed the water, hasn't
the rain rained?

141
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:18,000
De, wele baranê li vir rinde lê kirîye, ne?
 
Yes, by God, it has rained well here, hasn't it?

142
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:29,000
De ka avê wê din jî lêkin. Xwedê qebîl bike. Xwedê rehma xwe
lê ke. Û em dibên wê bardestokî ne, Xwedê rizqê te bide apê
Zêrevan.
 
Come on, pour the other water too. May God accept it. May
God have mercy on her. And we say may you have a helper, may
God provide for you uncle Zerevan.

143
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Û evê birakî ye. Me jî me re çaw darivînaye, hino ev dî ne
pêl tirbê me nin. Şebaba vî derê de şixulin.
 
And this brother of yours. He also looked for us... they
step on our graves. The youth are working in this area.

144
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Lo, baş erba pêş me dewsî? Me dewsî. De, pêş me dewsîne ewê
çerxê? Ê xwe birîn bikî.
 
Man, did we step on the front of the cart? We stepped on it.
Come on, didn't we step on the front of that wheel? It will
cut itself.

145
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Dorê sêc e, ew pir rind e. Binê xwe xweş e. Lêke hemû daxwe
lêvê jî ke, ka me diêşîne. Yeke vir de...
 
It's a triple layer, it's very nice. Its bottom is nice. Put
it, pour it all, so it doesn't hurt us. One here...

146
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Xwedê qebîl ke, Xwedê qebîl ke. Xwedê rehma xwe lêke... Ka
tepsoka hûn hildin em tiştekî amade bikin we bixwin.
 
May God accept it, may God accept it. May God have mercy...
Come on, pick up the shovel so we can prepare something for
you to eat.

147
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Beşar ka bêrek ax ê an kevirê wî têxe ser, lo.
 
Bashar, come on, put a shovel of dirt or a stone on it, man.

148
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Danin zû, da biki axê gundê, hicar lamîşkin.
 
Put it quickly, so they mix the soil of the village with
rocks.

149
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Tabî, xelkê me kesê xwe li vir tine ye. Da ka çikinin dar
çandine, ji bo rehmetyê xwe çandin e, kesê xwe li vir tine
ye. Em kelifandin em bi kerema xwe wecibê gund rabin ne?
 
Of course, our people have no relatives here. They are
planting trees, they planted them for their deceased, they
have no relatives here. We took the trouble to fulfill the
duty of the village out of our kindness, right?

150
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Ne wî? Ka axê bînin axê. Ewa.
 
Isn't it so? Come on, bring the dirt, the dirt. There.

151
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Emê axê gundê ha ceribînin.
 
We will try the soil of this village.

152
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Ka şûşeyek av jî lêkin. Lêkin.
 
Come on, pour a bottle of water on it. Pour it.

153
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Ka şûşek av bînin lêkin.
 
Come on, bring a bottle of water and pour it.

154
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Bes, hema şil bibe bes, Xwedê qebîl ke.
 
Enough, just let it get wet, that's enough, may God accept
it.

155
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Beşar bê pîşiya te di vir de pîs bibê ew dî tirba do. Ew bê
pîşî bena çiqa ev bi gi pîs bike. Xwedê qebîl bike ev e gî
pîs bike, ev e.
 
Bashar, your pants will get dirty here by the grave. Look,
his pants got dirty from all this mud. May God accept it,
look at all this mud, this is it.

156
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Rinde gel cem hev e am kî nuka dî jî hinek belavkin li
terbek din e hinek evê.
 
It's good that people are together, we will now distribute
some more to other graves, some of this.

157
00:19:54,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Dê berê xwe bidine iştê.
 
Come on, look at the work.

158
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Ko were Menco, were Menco.
 
Come Menco, come Menco.

159
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Baş e, tu çêkî, bi destê xwe bigire.
 
Okay, you do it, hold it with your hand.

160
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Ev sîm bona bibin evê?
 
Is this wire to take this?

161
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Na dîwar e kê... ma em neku bibin cihekî din...
 
No, it's a wall... so we don't take it somewhere else...

162
00:20:43,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Têke têke.
 
Put it in, put it in.

163
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Abu Ebdê, ev bêriya avê we kir... ma yê...?
 
Abu Abdo, you made this water pipe... is it...?

164
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Yekê avê bikî ko şevekê ava me biqe te eza...
 
To put water in one, so if one night our water cuts off
you...

165
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Abu Ebdê.
 
Abu Abdo.

